# `data/` — Data layer

All data lives here and is versioned with **{{ data_versioning }}**, not git.
Three stages, by how they are produced:

| Subfolder | Produced by | Editable? |
|-----------|-------------|:---------:|
| `raw/` | The instrument / the world | ⛔ immutable |
| `interim/` | Pipeline, mid-stream | ⛔ regenerated |
| `processed/` | Pipeline, analysis-ready (parquet/zarr) | ⛔ regenerated |

**Only `raw/` is irreplaceable.** `interim/` and `processed/` are cheap: they are
rebuilt by `snakemake` from `raw/` + code, so deleting them costs only compute. If
you ever feel the urge to hand-edit a file in `interim/` or `processed/`, the fix
belongs in the pipeline instead.

- Populate with `{{ data_versioning }} pull`; publish with `{{ data_versioning }} push`.
- Nothing in `data/` is committed to git except this README and `.gitignore`.

Immutability rules for `raw/` are in [`raw/README.md`](raw/README.md).
